// 7. EMBEDDED VIABILITY CERTIFIER — DSN-EVC-01
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

seed("embedded_viability_certifier") = {
  id:     "DSN-EVC-01",
  status: "design — security layer CONVERGED + S5-ratified 2026-06-04 (Claude@S3 ↔ Qwen@S4, 4 rounds); core spec pending",
  // debt(CITED-AXIOMS-NOT-ABSORBED, class=doc, owner=DS, gate=none)
  // ── ABSORBED PREMISES. 2026-08-09, per §cited_is_declared: an identifier
  //    CITED in system/ needs a declaration IN system/. These eight had a
  //    statement in a fuse source; they are carried here VERBATIM in meaning,
  //    with their origin, because a proof document that states its premises is
  //    more self-contained, ¬less.
  absorbed_premises = {
    Ax_AttestationSeparation:
      "attestation ≜ LOGICAL state (what V believes) ▪ reality check ≜ PHYSICAL
       state (what V observes). BOTH run; their DISAGREEMENT is itself the
       signal.                        ← kernel/attested_state_primitive"

    Ax_NoObscurity:
      "certifier OPEN ∧ REPRODUCIBLE. Tamper-resistance ≜ external sha +
       signature, ¬concealment.       ← kernel/embedded_viability_certifier"

    Ax_TwoLevelAttestation:
      "S5 ⊢ certifier_key (authorises the certifier) ∧ certifier ⊢
       instance_attestation(nonce, ts) (proves viability NOW; anti-replay).
                                      ← kernel/embedded_viability_certifier"

    Ax_SignedUpdateOnly:
      "a new covenant hash is adopted ONLY via an S5-signed version increment.
       Absence of the anchor ⟹ DEGRADE to last-known-good-signed, never halt.
       Local tamper ⟹ halt, but SCREAM FIRST.
                                      ← kernel/embedded_viability_certifier"

    Ax_SafeFallback:
      "missing telemetry ⟹ CONSERVATIVE operation. SAFE_MODE is tested, not
       assumed.                       ← spec/vsl_thermal_refinements_20260513"

    Def_SplitOperator:
      "x(t+1) = f₀(x(t)) + σ(t)·η(t)
         f₀ : ℝ¹²⁸ → ℝ¹²⁸  deterministic, asymmetric (encodes the hierarchy)
         η  ~ N(0, I₁₂₈)   isotropic, reversible by symmetry
         σ(t) ∈ [σ_min, σ_max]  driven by the Abreath cycle
                                      ← spec/vsm_notation_spec_addendum"

    Cor_GovernedDefinition:
      "governed(x_t) ≜ (x_t ∈ Ω) ∧ (mean E[ΔL] over the window ≤ 0)
                        ∧ (E[L(x_t)] within R)
                                      ← spec/vsm_notation_spec_addendum"

    Cor_ReframeRecertification:
      "after reframe() modifies parameters:
         1 re-estimate {ε₀, M, K_B, K_H, L_f} on the NEW operator
         2 check ∃ R s.t. the drift inequality holds
         3 wait τ_recert = 2·τ_rec for the transient to settle
                                      ← spec/vsm_notation_spec_addendum"
  }


    // ── CLASSIFIED 2026-08-09. The debt said "declared in a fuse source that
    // was never absorbed". Reading the sources, that is true of EIGHT and
    // FALSE of eleven, and the difference changes what the work IS.
    //
    // WITH a statement — absorbable, the fuse is real work but mechanical:
    //   Ax_AttestationSeparation ▪ Ax_NoObscurity ▪ Ax_SafeFallback
    //   Ax_SignedUpdateOnly ▪ Ax_TwoLevelAttestation ▪ Cor_GovernedDefinition
    //   Cor_ReframeRecertification ▪ Def_SplitOperator
    //
    // WITHOUT one — these were REVIEWED, REFINED and SIGNED OFF and never
    // WRITTEN. The corpus carries a review chain for statements that do not
    // exist:
    //   Ax_BinaryIntegrity ▪ Ax_BoundaryMatchedAuth ▪ Ax_CapabilityFallback
    //   Ax_ChainVirginity ▪ Ax_ChannelAuthentication ▪ Ax_CovenantAnchoring
    //   Ax_ManifestSigning ▪ Ax_ProgramIsolation ▪ Ax_TrustChainContinuity
    //   Cor_AlgedonicTrigger ▪ Ax_Aε
    // Ax_BinaryIntegrity is the shape of all of them: `(refined) …(external
    // check + scream-then-halt)` in one document, `accept //` in a review,
    // `scream-then-halt, never halt` in a signoff. Three texts ABOUT it, ∄
    // text that IS it.
    //
    // CONSEQUENCE, and it is why this classification had to precede the work:
    // an automated absorption would have imported REVIEW VERDICTS as axioms.
    // `Ax_BinaryIntegrity: accept` would have entered the canon as an axiom
    // whose statement is the word `accept`.
    //
    // Ax_Aε was ¬an orphan at all — it was the index truncating `Ax_Aε` to
    // `Ax_A` because the formal-identifier charset carried Ω ψ τ σ λ μ and not ε.
    // A truncated name looks exactly like a real orphan until someone opens
    // the line. Charset widened to the Greek block; the name now indexes whole
    // and is a genuine orphan, but a differently-named one.

  // TWENTY axioms are CITED by documents in system/ and DECLARED in ∄ one of
  // them. Each is declared in a FUSE SOURCE that was never absorbed:
  //   embedded_viability_certifier.vsm  — Ax_BinaryIntegrity ▪ Ax_NoObscurity
  //     ▪ Ax_ManifestSigning ▪ Ax_CovenantAnchoring ▪ Ax_ChannelAuthentication
  //     ▪ Ax_TrustChainContinuity ▪ Ax_TwoLevelAttestation
  //     ▪ Ax_BoundaryMatchedAuth ▪ Ax_SignedUpdateOnly
  //   vsl_thermal_refinements_20260513  — Ax_CapabilityFallback
  //     ▪ Ax_ProgramIsolation ▪ Ax_SafeFallback
  //   vsm_notation_spec_addendum        — Cor_AlgedonicTrigger
  //     ▪ Cor_GovernedDefinition ▪ Cor_ReframeRecertification
  //   autoimmune_test.spec ▪ response_classes ▪ masked_alerts_rca ▪ others
  //
  // This is the Ax_SplitOperator class, at scale. That one I found by
