    vs_manifest: "manifest DECLARES ▪ attestation CERTIFIES the same, produced by
      a RUNNING verifiable certifier.  manifest ≡ claim · attestation ≡ proof",
  },

  recursion: "the certifier IS the recursive invariant — V′ ⊃ V′ ⊃ V′, ∀ level
    running the SAME minimal certifier, exposing the SAME @connection_schema
    contract, now EXECUTING it.
    ⟹ recursion stops being a diagram ∧ becomes a running verifiable artifact",

  resolves: {
    // debt(COLD-START-TRUST, class=doc, owner=rmw3, gate=design_unresolved)
  // DSN-COUPLE-01's open gap, and it is a DESIGN question, ¬an implementation
  // one: what does a parent extend to an S1 it has never seen? Every current
  // answer assumes prior history. Blocks the coupling manifest's phase 4.
  cold_start_trust: "DSN-COUPLE-01's open gap — ¬trust an unknown S1's
      DECLARATION; verify its certifier's ATTESTATION, rooted in certifier
      binary identity. the sha-root IS the CA.
      quis custodiet ⟹ the certifier is verifiable, ¬self-trusted",
    vantage_problem: "∀ instance certifies ITSELF from inside ⟹ the parent needs
      ∄ vantage INTO opaque instances. S3* becomes bidirectional across the
      membrane: child self-audits ∧ presents, parent verifies",
    distributed_psi: "peer ψ-coupling = MUTUAL attestation exchange; coupling.rs Handshake becomes 'exchange + verify each other's Viability Attestation before ψ' — same protocol, horizontal",
  },

  security_hinge: "CRITICAL — a self-certifier CAN LIE.
  defense: parent verifies the CERTIFIER'S IDENTITY (binary sha + covenant
  signature), ¬its OUTPUT.
  self-certification ∖ verifiable trust root ≡ theater.
  root = covenant key / CA chain over certifier binaries",

  becomes_PSI: "PSI/1.0 (task O) ≢ an onboarding manifest — it is a VIABILITY
  ATTESTATION PROTOCOL: handshake ≡ attestation exchange + verification.
  the open standard by which ∀ viable system PROVES (¬declares) its viability
  to couple, recursively ∧ peer-to-peer",

  security_layer_converged: {
    foundation: [
      "M1 — security ≡ transparency ∧ attestability, ¬obfuscation
   (Kerckhoffs for viability certification). ∄ obfuscation ▪ ∄ anti-debug.
   tamper-resistance ← reproducible build + signed binary + EXTERNAL sha",
      "M2 — trust ROOT is OFFLINE: rmw3 pubkey + covenant hash baked in at build.
   the public anchor is freshness ∧ revocation ONLY (n01/bastion SPOF, R8).
   AUTHORITY ≡ S5 signature, never a URL ∨ a bare hash-match",
    ],
    axioms: [
      "Ax_NoObscurity: certifier OPEN + REPRODUCIBLE; tamper-resistance via external sha + signature",
      "Ax_SignedUpdateOnly: a new covenant hash is adopted ONLY via an S5-signed
     version increment. ∄ anchor ⟹ DEGRADE to last-known-good-signed, ¬halt.
     local tamper ⟹ halt, but SCREAM FIRST",
      "Ax_TwoLevelAttestation: S5 ⊢ certifier_key (authorizes certifier); certifier ⊢ instance_attestation(nonce, ts) (proves viability NOW; anti-replay)",
      "Ax_BoundaryMatchedAuth: signed Ed25519 challenge-response in-host (no PKI); mTLS only cross-node",
      "refined: Ax_CovenantAnchoring(offline root) · Ax_BinaryIntegrity(external check + scream-then-halt) · Ax_ManifestSigning(split S5-manifest / certifier-attestation) · Ax_ChannelAuthentication · Ax_TrustChainContinuity",
    ],
    spec_guards: [
      "G_repro (LOAD-BEARING): reproducibility ≡ the chain's premise ⟹ VERIFY BY
   REBUILD (twice on n02, byte-identical) BEFORE the CA.
   cargo --locked + source-date-epoch: necessary, ¬sufficient — also needs
   --remap-path-prefix ▪ pinned toolchain ▪ normalized debug info ▪ ∄ timestamps.
   tier_α.0",
      "G_keylife: the CA MUST specify key LIFECYCLE, ¬only topology —
   root custody (covenant/A4) ▪ certifier-key issuance ∧ rotation
   ▪ REVOCATION [promote to tier_α]",
      "G_genesis: BOTH ends embed the offline root at build time —
   parent ⊇ {S5 pubkey, canonical certifier sha}
   certifier ⊇ {S5 pubkey, covenant hash}
   ⟹ ∄ bootstrap hole ∧ ∄ network needed for first contact",
      "G_halt_screams: halt ⟹ emit α(sev10) + a final signed 'halting:tamper'
   attestation BEFORE halting. never die silently (anti-orphan lesson)",
    ],
    reuse: "A4 witness scaffolding (Ed25519-dalek, already in vsf-agent) · DSN-COUPLE-01 Phase 1 manifest + validator · covenant.vsm v1.1 + covenant_ops.vsm v0.1 (S5-signed)",
  },

  next: [
    "(0) G_repro REPRODUCIBILITY GATE first (verify-by-rebuild on n02)",
    "(1) Viability Attestation schema (extends coupling_manifest + signature)",
    "(2) minimal-certifier core spec (Ω + self-reconcile + governed + gate; no_std target = vsi.rs)",
    "(3) verification protocol (signature + certifier-sha CA + challenge/nonce)",
    "(4) trust-root / CA model over certifier binaries (covenant key chain)",
    "gated/related: vsi.rs, EXP-TRUST-01 (trust state IN attestation), covenant signing key, DSN-COUPLE-01 — natural successor to its Phase 4",
  ],
}

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// 8. RECURSIVE CHANNEL PROTOCOL — inter-level operational contract
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// origin: recursive_channel_protocol.vsm 2026-06-13 — answers: given a CHILD and
//   its PARENT, what flows between them, in what direction, under what constraints?
// derives D4, D11, A4, A5
//
// LEVEL INDICES REMOVED 2026-08-07 (claude_review). The source parametrised this
// as (V_a: level=N, V_b: level=N+1) with φ↑ : V_a → V_b, i.e. the PARENT carrying
// the HIGHER index — inverted against canon A1, S1(L) = {V_i(L+1)}, which puts the
// parent at the LOWER index (primer: read(V(L−1), φ↑(V(L))); kernel.rs:352:
// child = self.level + 1). The whole section shared the inversion, including the
// banking example, so it was a CONVENTION and ¬a typo. The fuse was faithful; the
// source contradicts A1.
// Named roles are immune to the convention — vsl_language D2/D3 use
// parent_of(V_i) and were never wrong. Same fix here.

channels(child, parent) = {           // parent = child's L − 1, per A1
  phi_up:     { direction: "child → parent.S3",  type: telemetry,   attenuation: true  },
  phi_down:   { direction: "parent.S3 → child",  type: parameters,  amplification: true },
  algedonic:  { direction: "child → parent.S5",  type: emergency,   bypass: true       },
  S2_lateral: { direction: "child ↔ sibling",    type: coordination, mediated: "parent.S2" },
  psi:        { direction: "child.S4 ↔ peer.S4", type: intelligence, preconditions: "D11" },
}
// S2_lateral and psi are NOT sibling-to-sibling direct links — both mediated by a third system

phi_up_contract = {
  carrier:   "telemetry/{system_id}/events.jsonl",
  signing:   "Ed25519 per event (Merkle-chained — AX-STATE)",
  direction: "child.S1 → parent.S3",
  semantics: "variety attenuation — the child reduces internal variety to signals meaningful at the parent's level of abstraction",
  content_classes: {
    metric_blocks: { description: "continuous operational telemetry",
      examples: [kernel, ingest, omega, lyapunov, vr, clock, variety],
      cadence:  "∀ tick (adaptive via W4)",
      consumer: "parent.S3 pattern recognition" },
    l2_class_executions: {
      description: "discrete events when a D4-L2 class fires",
      schema: { tick: "int", event_type: "\"l2_class_execution\"", class: "string ratified class name (e.g. lyapunov_trust_modulation)", trigger: "condition that fired the class", state_before: "relevant dims before", state_after: "relevant dims after" },
      requirement: "MANDATORY — every L2 class execution MUST emit this event type",
      rationale: "parent.S3 MUST distinguish background noise (metric_blocks) from
        discrete non-trivial actions (l2_class_executions). ∄ it ⟹ the causal
        structure is invisible: gradual drift vs discrete class firing",
    },
    algedonic_bypass: { description: "not delivered via events.jsonl" },
  },
  machine_readability: "φ↑ ≢ a log for humans — it is the SENSOR INPUT of
    parent.S3, which may be another nucleus running autonomously.
    ∀ content MUST parse without semantic interpretation; VSL-typed preferred",
}

phi_down_contract = {
  carrier:   "telemetry/{system_id}/params.json",
  direction: "parent.S3 → child",
  semantics: "policy amplification — adjusts the child's operating parameters
      within bounds child.S5 has PRE-authorized",
  sovereignty_boundary: {
    rule: "parent.S3 CANNOT override child.S5 policy via φ↓",
    adjustable:     ["VIABLE_THRESHOLD", "LYAP_R_CORE", "SIGMA_DRIFT_GAIN", "use_split_operator", "canon_interval_secs"],
    NOT_adjustable: ["covenant.vsm", "D4 class definitions", "A5 ceiling", "Omega constraint set", "Ed25519 signing key"],
    rationale: "∀ V has its OWN S5. the parent's S3 has OPERATIONAL authority over
      its S1 units, ¬POLICY authority. confusing the two collapses VSM into
      hierarchy ∧ eliminates recursion's autonomy.
      a regulator may adjust a bank's viability threshold, ¬rewrite its covenant",
    enforcement: "the child parses params.json into a TYPED struct;
      fields ∉ the pre-authorized schema are IGNORED.
      the struct is defined by child.S5, ¬by the parent",
  },
  d4_interaction: "φ↓ can ACTIVATE a pre-ratified D4-L2 class remotely (e.g. {use_split_operator: true}); CANNOT define a new class — class definition is D4-L3 (requires_human at child.S5)",
}

algedonic_contract = {
  carrier:   "NATS Core vsf.{vsf_id}.algedonic (sub-ms, no fsync)",
  direction: "any descendant → ancestor.S5 DIRECT",
  semantics: "BINARY emergency bypass — skips S3 aggregation entirely",
  properties: [
    "bypass: does not wait for φ↑ aggregation cycle",
    "priority: highest routing priority at carrier layer",
    "rate_limit: AlgedonicGate — max 2 per second per origin (ALG-1)",
    "decay: algedonic_decay(L,t) ≤ exp(−λ·t) prevents cascade saturation",
  ],
  recursive_semantics: "a critical event at any descendant reaches the S5 of its
    parent ▪ grandparent ▪ … simultaneously; ∀ level's AlgedonicGate decides
    INDEPENDENTLY whether to re-emit upward",
  cascade_rule: "re-emit upward ONLY if local_resolution_failed ∧ Δt > τ_L — prevents one leaf transient from paging every S5 in the recursion tree",
  banking_example: "a transaction unit detects topology-break ⟹ α to its parent
    (the bank) S5. unresolvable ∧ systemic ⟹ re-emit to the grandparent (the
    regulator) S5 after τ ⟹ the regulator sees the cascade ORIGIN, ¬its local
    symptom.
    // levels named by ROLE, ¬index: under A1 the regulator carries the LOWEST L
    // and the transaction unit the highest. The source had it the other way.",
}

s2_lateral_contract = {
  rule_A4: "NO direct sibling coupling; child ↔ sibling ALWAYS mediated by parent.S2",
  mediation: "NATS broker (LXC 106, role=S2). siblings submit → S2 routes ∧
      filters ∧ logs → parent.S3 observes the coordination channel",
  recursive_insight: {
    claim: "S2 at level N is ITSELF an S1 unit at level N+1",
    meaning: "the coordination system (SWIFT, interbank settlement, NATS broker)
      is a viable system in its own right — own S1..S5 ▪ own attractor ▪ own
      viability signal ⟹ a mature deployment gives it its own nucleus",
    implication: "governing the coordination layer is ¬optional.
      fail(S2) ∨ captured(S2) ⟹ the whole level loses coherence ⟹
      the coordinator MUST be as governed as the units it coordinates",
  },
}

psi_channel = {
  rule: "ψ(V_A, V_B): S4_A ↔ S4_B — intelligence exchange between governed systems",
  level: "S4 only (not S1, not S3 direct)",
  preconditions: [
    "governed(V_A) ∧ governed(V_B)",
    "trust(V_A, V_B) ≥ limited",
    "bilateral S5 approval (V_A.S5 ∧ V_B.S5)",
    "mediated: expansion_module ∘ handshake ∘ S3.filter",
  ],
  distinction_from_S2: "S2 lateral is WITHIN a tree (siblings, same parent); ψ is BETWEEN trees (V_A and V_B may have different parents). A4 applies within a tree; D11 governs cross-tree coupling",
  anti_capture: "ψ requires bilateral S5 approval + governing proof; a compromised or ungoverned V cannot open a ψ channel; the coupling preconditions ARE the resistance mechanism",
}

d4_cross_level = {
  insight: "D4-L1 (process_autonomous) vs D4-L2 (class_execution) has CROSS-LEVEL
    consequences, invisible when a system is considered in isolation",
  from_parent_S3: {
    L1_actions: "continuous background process; steady-state signal in metric_blocks; no special attention",
    D4_L2_actions: "discrete class execution ⟹ MUST be a typed event, ¬inferred
      from a metric change. ∄ l2_class_execution events ⟹ parent.S3 cannot
      distinguish trust falling from a D4-L2 class firing vs from D4-L1 drift",
  },
  implementation_requirement: "∀ D4-L2 class ratified at child.S5 MUST have a
    corresponding φ↑ event type, emitted AT execution, BEFORE the next
    metric_block ⟹ parent.S3 gets the causal ordering: class fires → metric Δ",
  classes_pending: ["lyapunov_trust_modulation (2026-06-13c, D4-L2)", "topology_response (2026-06-13c, D4-L2)"],
  // debt(D4L2-CLASSES-PENDING, class=kernel, owner=DS, gate=system_certified)
  // Two D4-L2 learning classes ratified 2026-06-13c and ¬wired. Both have a
  // mathematical footing (lyapunov_trust_modulation rests on Q2), so the
  // blocker is wiring, ¬theory. A ratified class that never fires is an
  // autonomy the system was granted and does not exercise.
}

channel_summary = {
  phi_up:     { "child→parent.S3",   direct,         "N/A",        "child controls content"   },
  phi_down:   { "parent.S3→child",   direct,         "D4-L2 gate", "child.S5 controls schema" },
  algedonic:  { "child→parent.S5",   AlgedonicGate,  "N/A",        "rate-limited, binary"     },
  S2_lateral: { "child↔sibling",     "parent.S2",    "A4",         "parent.S3 observes"       },
  psi:        { "child.S4↔peer.S4",  "expansion+S3", "D11",        "bilateral S5"             },
}

